#
# Copyright (c) 2026 William David Louth
#
# Perfkit runner configuration.
#
# Copy this file to jmh.env and edit it. Every runner loads jmh.env from the
# project directory before doing anything else, so a configured checkout runs
# with a bare command:
#
#   ./jmh.sh build
#   ./jmh.sh decision core
#
# rather than restating coordinates on every invocation. Create it with
# defaults by running:
#
#   ./jmh.sh env --init
#
# and see what a command will actually use, and where each value came from,
# with:
#
#   ./jmh.sh env
#
# jmh.env is untracked: it names the artifacts on one machine, not a property of
# the suite. Point elsewhere with JMH_ENV=/path/to/other.env to keep several
# configurations side by side.
#
# A variable already exported in the calling shell always wins over this file,
# so a one-off stays a one-off:
#
#   SPI_VERSION=1.1.0 ./jmh.sh build
#
# This file is sourced by bash. Use plain NAME=value assignments; quote values
# containing spaces. Nothing here is built from source — every coordinate below
# names an artifact that must already be resolvable by Maven.
#
# This suite's own version is not configurable here. It is a literal in
# pom.xml, bumped there when the suite is released, and it tracks the
# benchmarks rather than anything they measure.
#

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider under measurement (build time)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The three coordinates travel together: supplying SPI_ARTIFACT activates the
# provider dependency and requires the other two. Leaving all three unset builds
# a suite with no provider — benchmarks can be listed, but not run.
#
# These apply when the jar is assembled and have no effect afterwards; the
# assembled jar records what it measures.

SPI_GROUP=io.humainary.substrates
SPI_ARTIFACT=humainary-substrates-spi-alpha
SPI_VERSION=3.6.0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider selection (run time)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed when ServiceLoader would find no provider or several. The runners
# forward this to the forked JVM as -Dio.humainary.substrates.spi.provider.

# SPI_PROVIDER=io.humainary.substrates.spi.alpha.Provider

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# APIs measured through
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Versioned independently of this suite. Set these when measuring a provider
# built against an API release other than the pom's default.

# SUBSTRATES_API_VERSION=3.6.0
# SERVENTIS_API_VERSION=3.6.0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The VM benchmarks are measured under (run time)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every runner forwards this to the forked JVM. It defaults to
#
#   -server -Xms1g -Xmx1g -XX:+AlwaysPreTouch -XX:+UseG1GC
#
# which is stated rather than inherited because the host's own defaults are not
# a constant: heap sizing scales with the machine's memory, and on a host with
# one active processor ergonomics selects the serial collector instead of G1.
# Two machines running the same command with nothing set would otherwise be
# measuring under two different VMs, and for an allocation-heavy row that is a
# different experiment rather than a faster or slower one.
#
# Raise the heap for a workload whose live set does not fit a gigabyte, or name
# a different collector to measure against one. Setting it to nothing measures
# under whatever this host's ergonomics choose — worth seeing deliberately, not
# worth comparing across machines:
#
#   JMH_JVM_ARGS=

# JMH_JVM_ARGS="-server -Xms1g -Xmx1g -XX:+AlwaysPreTouch -XX:+UseG1GC"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Maven repository holding the artifacts above
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed when it is not ~/.m2/repository. Used by Maven during builds and
# to locate artifacts for the staleness check.

# MAVEN_REPO_LOCAL=$HOME/.m2/repository
